# The Docker build context is the repository root — see the Dockerfile header
# for why it cannot be scoped to mcp/.
#
# .git is deliberately absent from this file. mcp/scripts/build-content.mjs
# enumerates the content it bundles with `git ls-files`, so excluding .git
# would break the build, not just shrink the context.

# Dependency trees and build output are regenerated inside the image from
# package-lock.json and plugins/, so shipping the host's copies would only
# risk a stale or platform-wrong artifact leaking in.
**/node_modules
mcp/dist

# Generated at build time by build-content.mjs's copyRootLegalFile() from the
# root LICENSE/NOTICE, and git-ignored for that reason. The root originals
# are copied in by the Dockerfile; these would be overwritten anyway.
mcp/LICENSE
mcp/NOTICE

# Local tooling debris and caches. `git ls-files` already ignores untracked
# files when indexing content, so none of this could reach the bundle — but
# keeping it out of the context makes the build measurably faster.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/.DS_Store
**/*.pyc

# Agent scratch space, including nested git worktrees that would otherwise
# send an entire second checkout of this repo as build context.
.claude/worktrees

# Packaged bundles and archives — build products, never build inputs.
*.mcpb
*.tgz
